Cell["\<\
The four relations of a string algebra are the defining identities of an \
involutive bi-Lie algebra: the Jacobi identity of the bracket, the co-Jacobi \
identity of the co-bracket, their Drinfeld compatibility, and involutivity.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e41acbc2-237b-4a19-b5f5-22306b726be5"],

Cell["\<\
The relations of a string algebra do not depend on the convention of the \
pairing or on the empty word.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6033afb5-c6c2-4d38-9bc3-92d0e4c6cb99"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The arity ",
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b038dda-ff35-4497-89a6-2ec504e181fa"],
 " says that the relation is defined on every positive number of arguments: \
an A-infinity algebra has one relation of each arity, and so has a morphism. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["RelationsQ"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/RelationsQ", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c553be24-003e-48a4-ad00-43df0173e675"],
 " bounds the arity by the length of the tuples it tests."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a056d7f2-c40d-415c-a872-56a124d67b3c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The relations of a cochain complex with a pairing of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f14e3db-8a9c-43cd-aae6-b3dc02bb5cf7"],
 " are its axioms, each an identity on elements:"
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"27d1ec1e-3671-4259-94d0-9e534382efd1"],

